  "notes": "This release was originally printed with a misaligned Apple Records logo on the back, which was later corrected (see [r2498807] for example). The front cover photo is more tightly cropped than on other releases, showing less sky (noticeable over the roof tops right) and less of the drainage grating bottom right.\n\nAlso, Her Majesty was originally not printed on the side B label. This was added later (see [r6033667]). \n\nMatrix# on labels in parentheses.\n\nSmall Ⓟ on labels.\n\nB5 appears as \"Mean Mr Mustard\" on cover, but as \"Mean Mr. Mustard\" on label.\n\n[Back cover]:\nAn E.M.I. Recording. Thanks to George Martin, Geoff Emerick and Phillip McDonald\nPhotographs by Iain Macmillan\nPrinted by Garrod & Lofthouse International Ltd\n\n℗ 1969\nMfd. in U.K.\n\nPublishing:\n• Northern Songs - A1, A3, A4, A6, B2 to B11\n• Startling Music - A5\n• Harrisongs - A2, B1\n\nCopies exist with both black and white generic inners.\n\nRunouts are stamped.",
